{
  "__readme": "Shared parity fixtures for the versioned evaluation contract. Loaded by sdk/tests/score-contract-parity.test.ts in mcpjam-inspector (Zod: scoreResultSchema / resolvedScoreDefinitionSchema / evaluationConfigSnapshotSchema in sdk/src/contract/schemas.ts) AND, VERBATIM, by tests/convex/scoreContractParity.test.ts in mcpjam-backend (the hand-mirrored v.* validators in convex/lib/scoreContract.ts, exercised through the real ingest mutation boundary). The backend cannot import @mcpjam/sdk into convex/ default-runtime code, so this file is the only common ground truth — copy it byte for byte, do not re-author it. LOAD RULE: strip EVERY key whose name starts with '__' before handing a row to a validator; they are fixture annotations (__label, __why, __kind) and both validators reject unknown fields. DISPATCH: '__kind' selects which validator a row is for — 'result', 'definition', or 'snapshot'. The __digests block pins LITERAL hash constants produced by the SDK implementation; the backend asserts its own canonical-JSON + SHA-256 twin reproduces them exactly, rather than recomputing an expectation on both sides (which would prove only that each side agrees with itself). If a digest assertion fails, the two canonicalizations have drifted — STOP, do not edit the constants. When the contract shape changes, edit BOTH validator files AND this fixture in the same PR.",

