    "__readme": "PINNED CROSS-RUNTIME HASH CONSTANTS. Each `definitions` row holds an AUTHORED ScoreDefinition (onError/onSkipped may be absent) and the definitionHash it must produce AFTER resolution — that is what proves an omitted default and an explicit default hash identically. Each `configs` row holds authored definitions and the evaluationConfigHash of the resolved set. Both sides compute; neither side recomputes the expectation.",

    "definitions": [
      {
        "__label": "D1 — defaults OMITTED",
        "definition": {
          "scorerId": "refund-mentioned",
          "idSource": "explicit",
          "scorerVersion": "1",
          "implementationHash": "impl-refund-predicate-v1",
          "deterministic": true,
          "passThreshold": 1,
          "role": "gating"
        },
        "definitionHash": "c9ff5b95e1bf2ac3c30df469ee6c504b8384c01ececcb5cd1158d130b06e4818"
      },
      {
        "__label": "D2 — defaults EXPLICIT (must equal D1)",
        "__why": "Defaults-equivalence. Hashing an unresolved definition would make spelling out a default read as an evaluation-config change and flag every case as configChanged.",
        "definition": {
          "scorerId": "refund-mentioned",
          "idSource": "explicit",
          "scorerVersion": "1",
          "implementationHash": "impl-refund-predicate-v1",
          "deterministic": true,
          "passThreshold": 1,
