  "__verdicts": {
    "__readme": "PINNED CROSS-RUNTIME VERDICT ARITHMETIC for `allGatingScorersPassed` — the function the score contract becomes AUTHORITATIVE with at grading mode `enforce`. The inspector's copy lives in sdk/src/contract/derive.ts and decides an iteration's `result`; the backend's hand-mirror lives in convex/lib/scoreContract.ts and VERIFIES that reported result against the rows that were actually persisted. Two implementations of \"did the gates hold\" is exactly how a hosted run and a CI gate end up disagreeing about the same rows, so both sides run these cases. SHAPE: `definitions` are AUTHORED (onError/onSkipped may be absent — each side resolves them, which is also what proves an omitted default and an explicit one behave identically). `rows` name their definition by `scorerId`; each side stamps the resolved `definitionHash` onto the row before calling, because the join is BY HASH and hard-coding hashes here would duplicate what the __digests block already pins. A row whose scorerId matches no definition is intentionally left unjoinable. `expected` is `{passed, disagreeing, unresolved}` with both id lists sorted.",
    "cases": [
      {
        "__label": "V1 — every gating scorer scored and passed",
